# QA fail - send apps back to development

<!-- prism:qa-fail-contract:v1 -->

Use this skill when an app of a feature failed QA. The app returns to development: its Delivery evidence, every QA row that
names it and its Release rows move to `## Evidence history`, and a later `/dev-done` delivers it again.

## Usage

`/qa-fail [F-XXX] app [app ...]`

## Read-only preflight

When available, use:

```text
prism wiki transition-preflight F-XXX [path] --action qa-fail --json
```

Accept it only with common envelope schema 1, command facts, capability version 3 and an action-specific `qa-fail`
surface, transition version 2 and a consistent snapshot. Otherwise fall back to direct-file checks. The preflight is
copy-only and never authorizes a write.

## Supported action

`in-dev` + `dev`, `ready-for-qa` + `qa`, `in-qa` + `qa` or `ready-for-release` + `release` -> `in-dev` + `dev`

Each named app is at `ready-for-qa`, `in-qa` or `ready-for-release` (`app_stage_mismatch`). An app that is already released
changes through a bug fix or a reopen, never through `qa-fail`.

## Evidence and confirmation

Read `knowledge/wiki/SCHEMA.md`, `knowledge/wiki/LIFECYCLE.md`, `knowledge/wiki/ACTIONS.md`, `status-board.md`, the complete feature, its requirement
pages and API contract, and every bug page of the feature.

Each named app needs a failure on record (`qa_failure_unsupported`): a `fail` or `blocked` QA row in its current attempt, or a
linked bug. A linked bug is listed under `- Linked bugs:` of the history entry, belongs to the feature, lists the app, is
`open`, `in-fix` or `fixed`, and is not deferred. Record the failure first with `/qa-verify`, or create the bug in
this proposal (a new `open` + `dev` page under `knowledge/wiki/bugs/`).

The proposal, in one write:

- removes from the active tables, for each named app, its Delivery evidence row, every QA row that names it (an app row or an
  integration row) and its Release rows, and copies each verbatim under `- Archived evidence:` of one new
  `### <today> - qa-fail` entry in `## Evidence history`, as a table row that starts with its section name
  (`Delivery evidence`, `QA verification` or `Release`);
- removes the `pending` or `failed` Release row of every other app that is not released and took part in an archived
  integration row, archives it the same way and lists the app under `- Participants:` (its Delivery evidence and its app QA
  rows stay);
- fills the entry's `- Reason:`, `- Affected apps:` (the named apps), `- Affected tracks: none`, `- Reaffirmed evidence: none`,
  `- Requirement/API invalidations:` (one `path: done -> in-progress` line for each requirement page of a named app that was
  `done`, and `path: implemented -> agreed` for an API contract that was `implemented`) and `- Linked bugs:`;
- sets the requirement pages of the named apps from `done` to `in-progress` and an `implemented` API contract to `agreed`
  (change only `status` in those pages);
- adds `implementation`, `tests`, `qa` and `release` to the named apps in `app-revalidation`, and `qa` and `release` to each
  participant;
- sets the feature to `in-dev` + `dev`.

Show the complete write set. Reread the source and context immediately before confirmation and once again after it. After
explicit confirmation write the pages, the status board row and a `log.md` entry. If a multi-file write is partial, report the
exact observed changes and stop for fresh recovery; no transaction is implied. Decline or cancel means no mutation.

## Rules

- write-capable skill
- the history entry is append-only; never rewrite an earlier entry
- an archived row is copied exactly; a row that is archived and still active is `evidence_still_active`
- write current-state pages: replace superseded content in place, state rationale as a current fact and keep history in `log.md` and the records; mark each claim `**Decided:**`, `**Observed:**`, `**Proposed:**` or `**Assumed:**` (gaps stay in the Open questions table) and link the evidence of every Decided and Observed claim: the processed intake item, a record or a URL (see Evidence labels in the wiki schema)

## Output behavior

Return:

- feature and the apps sent back, with the failure that supports each
- the rows archived and the participants that lost a Release row
- the pages whose status changed
- the feature's new status

## Error and stop conditions

- if the feature file does not exist, return a clean missing-feature response
- if an app has no failure on record, stop and ask the tester to record it with `/qa-verify`
- if the user wants to cancel, stop without writing
